      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5361",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{10} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right).$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-5361.json",
