          "question": "e-5362",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3,$ we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{9}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{3}{5} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6 & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3).$",
